#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =====================================================================
# rvtests  -  run the official riscv-tests suite against the tutorial CPUs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# riscv-tests is the reference per-instruction test suite: for every
# instruction in the ISA it checks the normal cases, the corner cases,
# the source/destination aliasing cases (rd == rs1, rs1 == rs2, rd == x0)
# and -- the part a pipeline cares about -- the same operation re-run
# with 0, 1 and 2 nops between producer and consumer.
#
#   tools/rvtests                       # default core, whole suite
#   tools/rvtests --core all            # every core, matrix summary
#   tools/rvtests --core pipe add sra   # just these tests
#   tools/rvtests --trace rv32ui-add    # one test, cycle-by-cycle
#   tools/rvtests --list
#
# The suite itself is fetched on first use into third_party/riscv-tests
# (gitignored). What lives in this repo is the *environment* the tests
# run in -- tests/riscv-tests/env/ -- because riscv-tests deliberately
# leaves that to the target; see docs/40-riscv-tests.md.
#
# Requires: iverilog, vvp, riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc/objcopy/objdump, git.
# =====================================================================
